        <detaileddescription>
<para>LiveLoc indicates whether the dominating assignment in StackHomeValue (<ref refid="classanonymous__namespace_02_assignment_tracking_analysis_8cpp_03_1_1_assignment_tracking_lowering_1a4012a71c02f4a13c5234aea48e772f4cadba5553473d129a7985fb532dc249ff4" kindref="member">LocKind::Mem</ref>), DebugValue (<ref refid="classanonymous__namespace_02_assignment_tracking_analysis_8cpp_03_1_1_assignment_tracking_lowering_1a4012a71c02f4a13c5234aea48e772f4ca5988c20a047cfe063999787584b0aca7" kindref="member">LocKind::Val</ref>), or neither (<ref refid="classanonymous__namespace_02_assignment_tracking_analysis_8cpp_03_1_1_assignment_tracking_lowering_1a4012a71c02f4a13c5234aea48e772f4ca6adf97f83acf6453d4a6a4b1070f3754" kindref="member">LocKind::None</ref>) is valid, in that order of preference. This cannot be derived by inspecting DebugValue and StackHomeValue due to the fact that there&apos;s no distinction in <ref refid="structanonymous__namespace_02_assignment_tracking_analysis_8cpp_03_1_1_assignment_tracking_lowering_1_1_assignment" kindref="compound">Assignment</ref> (the class) between whether an assignment is unknown or a merge of multiple assignments (both are Status::NoneOrPhi). In other words, the memory location may well be valid while both DebugValue and StackHomeValue contain Assignments that have a <ref refid="struct_status" kindref="compound">Status</ref> of NoneOrPhi. Indexed by <ref refid="namespacellvm_1a8c9d5a3046b96979a032c218e858cd15" kindref="member">VariableID</ref>. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
